  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ankit Patel vs State Of U.P. And 4 Others on 28 February, 2023 Author: Surya Prakash Kesarwani Bench: Surya Prakash Kesarwani High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 3 Case :- Writ - C No. - 36873 of 2022 Petitioner :- Ankit Patel Respondent :- State Of U.P. And 4 Others Counsel for Petitioner :- Parvez Iqbal Ansari",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the impugned order dated 03.06.2022, although appealable under Section 70 of the Food Safety Standards Act, 2006; yet the writ petition is maintainable inasmuch as the impugned order has been passed without confronting the petitioner with the enquiry report and without affording any opportunity of hearing. He, therefore, submits that the impugned order is in breach of principals of natural justice and deserves to be interfered with by this Court. Shri Amit Manohar, learned Additional Chief Standing Counsel submits that the petitioner may approach the respondent no.3, who shall pass an order afresh in accordance with law after confronting the petitioner with the relied upon materials/report of the Food Safety Officer, Ballia dated 27.01.2022.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the impugned order dated 03.06.2022, although appealable under Section 70 of the Food Safety Standards Act, 2006; yet the writ petition is maintainable inasmuch as the impugned order has been passed without confronting the petitioner with the enquiry report and without affording any opportunity of hearing. He, therefore, submits that the impugned order is in breach of principals of natural justice and deserves to be interfered with by this Court. Shri Amit Manohar, learned Additional Chief Standing Counsel submits that the petitioner may approach the respondent no.3, who shall pass an order afresh in accordance with law after confronting the petitioner with the relied upon materials/report of the Food Safety Officer, Ballia dated 27.01.2022.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
